{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '175,233p' packages/axylo/src/public.ts && cat packages/axylo/src/messages/index.ts && cat packages/axylo/test/messages/index.test.ts && cat apps/docs/data/messages.mjs && sed -n '1,52p' apps/docs/pages/accessibility.md\"","aggregated_output":"  message: string;\n  /** The chart it came from: its title, else its element id. */\n  chart: string;\n  /** Where applicable. A diagnostic about the chart as a whole (no title, low contrast) has neither. */\n  field?: string;\n  /** First offending row indexes in the caller's own data, capped at 10. */\n  rows?: readonly number[];\n  count?: number;\n}\n\n/** Runs normalization and validation only. Works without a DOM, so a server or an agent can check options before rendering. */\n\n/** Built-in text. Templates use {name} placeholders. Every entry can be replaced through `messages` (spec A10). */\nexport interface Messages {\n  viewAsTable: string; hideTable: string;\n  noData: string; noObservation: string; incompleteStack: string;\n  moreRows: string; otherSlices: string;\n  valuesNotShown: string; valuesChanged: string; labelsHidden: string;\n  loading: string; empty: string; error: string; internalError: string;\n  chartName: string; chartSummary: string; seriesSummary: string; timeZoneNote: string;\n  plotLabel: string; controlsLabel: string; pointOf: string;\n  zoomIn: string; zoomOut: string; resetZoom: string; pause: string; resume: string;\n  previousPage: string; nextPage: string; pageOf: string; jumpToX: string;\n  /** Column headers and nouns. */\n  category: string; percentage: string; series: string; value: string;\n  /** Chart type names used in generated names and summaries. */\n  typeLine: string; typeArea: string; typeBar: string; typeScatter: string; typeDonut: string;\n  /** Summary sentences that have no cartesian form. */\n  donutSummary: string; seriesNoData: string; seriesNotDrawn: string; referenceLine: string; referenceBand: string;\n  /** What the keyboard proxy says it is (\"{type} chart\") and how it reads a position. */\n  plotRole: string; pointAll: string; seriesValue: string; position: string;\n  /** Label of the stack total in tooltips. */\n  total: string;\n  /** Single-click panning (WCAG 2.5.7), the table's \"Jump to\" when nothing matches, and how to move in the plot. */\n  panLeft: string; panRight: string; jumpNotFound: string; plotInstructions: string;\n  /** Toolbar toggle: while it is on, two clicks in the plot set the two ends of the zoom range (the non-dragging way to select a range, WCAG 2.5.7). */\n  selectRange: string;\n  /** A stack whose components have mixed signs: both ends, in place of one total ('{positive} and {negative}'). */\n  totalMixed: string;\n  /** Incomplete stacks in a summary: named when few ('{label}: incomplete at {positions}.'), counted when many ('{label}: {count} incomplete stacks.'). */\n  incompleteAt: string; incompleteCount: string;\n  /** Fills `{seeTable}` in `valuesNotShown`, `valuesChanged`, `labelsHidden` and `seriesNotDrawn` when the chart has a table; without one the placeholder is removed. An override without the placeholder is used as written. */\n  seeTable: string;\n}\nimport type { DatumRef, Formatters, Lookup } from '../core/contracts';\nimport type { Messages } from '../public';\n\nconst chartSummary = '{type} chart with {seriesCount} series. {xLabel} from {xMin} to {xMax}.';\n// chartSummary and the range, written out: no work at import time.\nconst fullChartSummary = '{type} chart with {seriesCount} series. {xLabel} from {xMin} to {xMax}. {yLabel} from {yMin} to {yMax}.';\nconst donutSlice = '{label}: {value} ({percent}).';\n\nexport const defaultMessages: Messages = {\n  viewAsTable: 'View as table',\n  hideTable: 'Hide table',\n  noData: 'No data',\n  noObservation: 'No observation',\n  incompleteStack: 'incomplete',\n  moreRows: '+{count} more',\n  otherSlices: 'Other ({count})',\n  valuesNotShown: 'Values not shown: {count}. {seeTable}',\n  valuesChanged: 'Values shown differently from the data: {count}. {seeTable}',\n  labelsHidden: 'Some labels hidden. {seeTable}',\n  loading: 'Loading chart.',\n  empty: 'No data to show.',\n  error: 'The chart could not be drawn.',\n  internalError: 'Something went wrong while drawing the chart.',\n  chartName: '{type} chart of {y} by {x}',\n  chartSummary: fullChartSummary,\n  seriesSummary: '{series}: minimum {min}, maximum {max}, last {last}.',\n  timeZoneNote: 'Times are shown in {zone}.',\n  plotLabel: 'Chart plot',\n  controlsLabel: 'Chart controls',\n  pointOf: '{series}, {x}, {value}. Point {index} of {count}.',\n  zoomIn: 'Zoom in',\n  zoomOut: 'Zoom out',\n  resetZoom: 'Reset zoom',\n  pause: 'Pause',\n  resume: 'Resume',\n  previousPage: 'Previous page',\n  nextPage: 'Next page',\n  pageOf: 'Page {page} of {count}',\n  jumpToX: 'Jump to {x}',\n  category: 'Category',\n  percentage: 'Percentage',\n  series: 'Series',\n  value: 'Value',\n  typeLine: 'Line',\n  typeArea: 'Area',\n  typeBar: 'Bar',\n  typeScatter: 'Scatter',\n  typeDonut: 'Donut',\n  donutSummary: '{type} chart with {count} slices. Total {total}.',\n  seriesNoData: '{series}: no data.',\n  seriesNotDrawn: '{series} could not be drawn. {seeTable}',\n  referenceLine: 'Reference line {label} at {from}.',\n  referenceBand: 'Reference band {label} from {from} to {to}.',\n  plotRole: '{type} chart',\n  pointAll: '{x}. {values}. {position}',\n  seriesValue: '{series} {value}',\n  position: 'Point {index} of {count}',\n  total: 'Total',\n  panLeft: 'Pan left',\n  panRight: 'Pan right',\n  jumpNotFound: 'No row matches {x}. Example: {example}',\n  plotInstructions: 'Left and right arrows move between points, up and down between series, and Enter selects. Plus and minus zoom; 0 resets.',\n  selectRange: 'Select range',\n  seeTable: 'See table.',\n  totalMixed: '{positive} and {negative}',\n  incompleteAt: '{label}: incomplete at {positions}.',\n  incompleteCount: '{label}: {count} incomplete stacks.',\n};\n\nexport function fill(template: string, values: Readonly<Record<string, string | number>>): string {\n  return template.replace(/\\{(\\w+)\\}/g, (placeholder: string, name: string) =>\n    Object.hasOwn(values, name) ? String(values[name]) : placeholder,\n  );\n}\n\nconst authoredMessages = new WeakMap<Messages, ReadonlySet<keyof Messages>>();\n\nexport function resolveMessages(overrides?: Partial<Messages> | null): Messages {\n  const messages = { ...defaultMessages };\n  const authored = new Set<keyof Messages>();\n  for (const key of Object.keys(messages) as (keyof Messages)[]) {\n    const value = overrides?.[key];\n    if (value == null) continue;\n    messages[key] = value;\n    authored.add(key);\n  }\n  authoredMessages.set(messages, authored);\n  return messages;\n}\n\nexport function messageLanguage(messages: Messages, key: keyof Messages): 'en' | null {\n  return messages[key] === defaultMessages[key] && !authoredMessages.get(messages)?.has(key) ? 'en' : null;\n}\n\nexport function fillChartSummary(\n  template: string, values: Readonly<Record<string, string>>, range: { readonly yMin: string; readonly yMax: string } | null,\n): string {\n  if (range) return fill(template, { ...values, ...range });\n  // When a translation uses the same placeholders, omit the sentence that would describe the missing range.\n  const withoutRange = template === fullChartSummary ? chartSummary\n    : template.match(/[^.!?。！？]+[.!?。！？]*|[.!?。！？]+/gu)?.filter(part => !/\\{y(?:Min|Max)\\}/.test(part)).join('').trim();\n  return fill(withoutRange || chartSummary, values);\n}\n\nexport function fillDonutSlice(label: string, value: string, percent: string): string {\n  return fill(donutSlice, { label, value, percent });\n}\n\nexport function pointOf(lookup: Lookup, ref: DatumRef, formatters: Formatters, messages: Messages): string | null {\n  const ordinal = lookup.ordinal(ref);\n  if (ordinal < 0) return null;\n  const datum = lookup.datum(ref);\n  if (!datum) return null;\n  return fill(messages.pointOf, {\n    series: datum.seriesLabel, x: datum.x, value: datum.value,\n    index: formatters.count(ordinal + 1), count: formatters.count(lookup.count),\n  });\n}\nimport { expect, it } from 'vitest';\nimport type { Messages } from '../../src/public';\nimport { defaultMessages, fill, resolveMessages } from '../../src/messages';\n\nit('gives every public message a non-empty default', () => {\n  const keys: Record<keyof Messages, true> = {\n    viewAsTable: true, hideTable: true, noData: true, noObservation: true, incompleteStack: true,\n    moreRows: true, otherSlices: true, valuesNotShown: true, valuesChanged: true, labelsHidden: true,\n    loading: true, empty: true, error: true, internalError: true,\n    chartName: true, chartSummary: true, seriesSummary: true, timeZoneNote: true,\n    plotLabel: true, controlsLabel: true, pointOf: true,\n    zoomIn: true, zoomOut: true, resetZoom: true, pause: true, resume: true,\n    category: true, percentage: true, series: true, value: true,\n    typeLine: true, typeArea: true, typeBar: true, typeScatter: true, typeDonut: true,\n    plotRole: true, pointAll: true, seriesValue: true, position: true, total: true,\n    panLeft: true, panRight: true, jumpNotFound: true, plotInstructions: true, selectRange: true, seeTable: true, totalMixed: true, incompleteAt: true, incompleteCount: true,\n    donutSummary: true, seriesNoData: true, seriesNotDrawn: true, referenceLine: true, referenceBand: true,\n    previousPage: true, nextPage: true, pageOf: true, jumpToX: true,\n  };\n  expect(Object.keys(defaultMessages).sort()).toEqual(Object.keys(keys).sort());\n  for (const text of Object.values(defaultMessages)) expect(text.trim()).not.toBe('');\n});\n\nit('fills templates once, preserving unknown names and literal braces and dollar signs in values', () => {\n  expect(fill('{series} at {index} ({series}) {missing} {toString}', { series: '{index} $&', index: 2 }))\n    .toBe('{index} $& at 2 ({index} $&) {missing} {toString}');\n});\n\nit('includes the table guidance placeholder in all four default templates', () => {\n  expect(defaultMessages).toMatchObject({\n    valuesNotShown: 'Values not shown: {count}. {seeTable}',\n    valuesChanged: 'Values shown differently from the data: {count}. {seeTable}',\n    labelsHidden: 'Some labels hidden. {seeTable}',\n    seriesNotDrawn: '{series} could not be drawn. {seeTable}',\n    seeTable: 'See table.',\n  });\n});\n\nit('replaces individual messages without changing defaults or copying undefined', () => {\n  const messages = resolveMessages({ noData: 'Keine Daten', loading: undefined });\n  expect(messages).toEqual({ ...defaultMessages, noData: 'Keine Daten' });\n  expect(defaultMessages.noData).toBe('No data');\n  expect(fill(messages.moreRows, { count: 3 })).toBe('+3 more');\n});\n// Where the chart shows each built-in message, for the generated messages table of the options reference\n// (pages/options.md). The table's keys and English text come from the library's own `defaultMessages`\n// (packages/axylo/src/messages/index.ts); the build fails when a key has no entry here or an entry names no\n// key, and test/options.test.ts checks that `defaultMessages` has exactly the keys of the public `Messages`.\n// Each entry was written from the place in packages/axylo/src that uses the key. Markdown.\n\nexport const messageUses = {\n  viewAsTable: 'The toolbar\\'s table control while the table is closed.',\n  hideTable: 'The same control while the table is open.',\n  noData: 'A value that is `null`, missing or not a number: in the tooltip, the table and the plot\\'s value text.',\n  noObservation: 'A series with no row at that x (line, area and bar), distinct from `noData`: in the tooltip, the table and the plot\\'s value text.',\n  incompleteStack: 'Marks a stack that is missing a part (area and bar): after its total in the tooltip and value text, and after its x in the table.',\n  moreRows: 'The last line of a tooltip or readout strip that cannot list every row.',\n  otherSlices: 'The donut slice that groups the slices past the seventh ([AX121](diagnostics.md#ax121)).',\n  valuesNotShown: 'The note in the figure, and a sentence of the summary, when values were left out.',\n  valuesChanged: 'The note and a summary sentence when values are drawn differently from the data (zeros for missing values, grouped slices, a default format).',\n  labelsHidden: 'The note in the figure when labels still do not fit after every remedy ([AX143](diagnostics.md#ax143)).',\n  loading: 'In place of the plot with `state: \\'loading\\'`.',\n  empty: 'In place of the plot when there are no rows, or with `state: { empty }` and no text of your own.',\n  error: 'In place of the plot when the chart cannot be drawn (an error diagnostic), or with `state: { error }` and no text of your own.',\n  internalError: 'In place of the plot after [AX199](diagnostics.md#ax199).',\n  chartName: 'The generated accessible name of a chart with neither `title` nor `labelledBy` ([AX140](diagnostics.md#ax140)).',\n  chartSummary: 'The first sentence of the summary, the figure\\'s description: type, number of series, x range and value range (line, area, bar, scatter, compact). Without a value range the sentence that would hold it is left out.',\n  seriesSummary: 'One summary sentence per series: its minimum, maximum and last value.',\n  timeZoneNote: 'The summary sentence that names the time zone of instants.',\n  plotLabel: 'The plot\\'s accessible name (the keyboard control laid over the plot).',\n  controlsLabel: 'The toolbar\\'s accessible name.',\n  pointOf: 'The plot\\'s value text for one series: on scatter, and after Up or Down on line, area and bar.',\n  zoomIn: 'A toolbar button, where the chart zooms (date, time and number x; see [zoom](updating.md#zoom)).',\n  zoomOut: 'A toolbar button, where the chart zooms; unavailable at full view.',\n  resetZoom: 'A toolbar button, once zoomed.',\n  pause: 'A toolbar button, once the chart has been appended to.',\n  resume: 'The same button while paused.',\n  previousPage: 'The table\\'s pager, above 100 rows.',\n  nextPage: 'The table\\'s pager, above 100 rows.',\n  pageOf: 'The table\\'s pager: where you are.',\n  jumpToX: 'The label of the table\\'s \"Jump to\" field, with the x column\\'s name.',\n  category: 'The first column header of a donut\\'s table, and the x part of a donut\\'s generated name.',\n  percentage: 'The share column header of a donut\\'s table.',\n  series: 'The series column header of a scatter chart\\'s table.',\n  value: 'The value axis title when several y fields share the axis and no name fits them all; the value part of a generated name when nothing else names it.',\n  typeLine: 'The chart type in the generated name and summary, and in the plot\\'s role description.',\n  typeArea: 'As `typeLine`, for area charts.',\n  typeBar: 'As `typeLine`, for bar charts.',\n  typeScatter: 'As `typeLine`, for scatter charts.',\n  typeDonut: 'As `typeLine`, for donuts.',\n  donutSummary: 'The first sentence of a donut\\'s summary.',\n  seriesNoData: 'The summary sentence for a series with no value to draw.',\n  seriesNotDrawn: 'The summary sentence for a series that cannot be drawn ([AX108](diagnostics.md#ax108)), and in place of the plot when no series can be.',\n  referenceLine: 'The summary sentence for a reference line.',\n  referenceBand: 'The summary sentence for a reference band.',\n  plotRole: 'The plot\\'s role description, with the chart type.',\n  pointAll: 'The plot\\'s value text with every visible series at one x (line, area and bar), and for a donut slice.',\n  seriesValue: 'One series\\' part of that value text, and the stack total\\'s.',\n  position: 'The position part of the value text.',\n  total: 'The label of a stack\\'s total in the tooltip and the value text.',\n  panLeft: 'A toolbar button once zoomed: half a view to the left; unavailable at the start.',\n  panRight: 'A toolbar button once zoomed: half a view to the right; unavailable at the end.',\n  jumpNotFound: 'Under the table\\'s \"Jump to\" field when no row matches, with an example of the column\\'s format.',\n  plotInstructions: 'The plot\\'s accessible description: how to move in it.',\n  selectRange: 'The name, and the `title`, of the Select range toggle after Zoom in, drawn as a symbol where the chart zooms: while it is pressed, two clicks on the plot set the two ends of the zoom range.',\n  seeTable: 'Fills `{seeTable}` in `valuesNotShown`, `valuesChanged`, `labelsHidden` and `seriesNotDrawn` when the chart has a table; without one the placeholder is removed.',\n  totalMixed: 'A stack total with parts of both signs, in the tooltip and the value text: both ends, in place of one total.',\n  incompleteAt: 'A compact area or bar chart\\'s summary: the stacks missing a part, named when there are three or fewer.',\n  incompleteCount: 'The same, counted when there are more than three.',\n};\n# Accessibility\n\nAfter this page you know what an Axylo chart exposes to assistive technology, to the keyboard and to readers with low vision, high-contrast settings or a colour-vision deficiency; which keys do what; how values are read with a pointer; what you as the author must supply; and what has and has not been verified.\n\nThese features are on by default: there is no module to import and no option to turn on.\n\n## What the chart provides\n\n| For | What the chart provides |\n|---|---|\n| Assistive technology | The figure is a group with an accessible name (`title`, or the heading named by `labelledBy`, or a generated name) and a description: the generated summary of type, series, x range with its time zone, value range, each series' minimum, maximum and last value, and anything left out. A compact chart is an image with the same name and description. The plot is one native range input whose value text describes the point in focus: its x, the value of each visible series with its unit, and its position (\"Point 4 of 120\"). Changes of state (loading, empty, error) are written once to a polite live region. \"View as table\" opens the data as an HTML table with a caption, column headers with units, and row headers. |\n| Keyboard | Up to two tab stops while the table is closed: the plot, and the toolbar when the chart has controls. A compact chart has none. Every point is reachable in order, the series can be switched, the ends are one key away, and Tab leaves the chart. The focus indicator is at least 2 px wide, in the focus colour, which meets 3:1 on the default backgrounds; it always shows while you use the keyboard in the plot, and it may also show after a click. |\n| Low vision | Text is HTML at 12 px or more by default, with 4.5:1 contrast for text and 3:1 for marks, axes and focus indicators in the default colours. Text follows browser zoom and the page's text-spacing settings. Labels never overlap; when one cannot be shown, the chart says so. The tooltip is placed against the marks it describes, not at the pointer, and does not cover them, a control or the focus ring; in a small plot its content is written in a strip under the plot instead (see [Reading values with a pointer](#reading-values-with-a-pointer)). |\n| Colour-vision deficiency | Eight colours chosen to stay apart under simulated protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia, and never colour alone: lines and areas carry marker shapes, repeated in the legend and tooltip; bars by position and order, named in the legend and tooltip, and also by fill pattern past the eighth series and between neighbours in a compact chart, which has no legend; adjacent fills are separated by background. |\n| High contrast | In forced-colours mode the chart uses system colours, and lines also differ by dash; so they do under `prefers-contrast: more`. |\n| Reduced motion | Nothing is animated on first render. Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` nothing transitions at all. |\n| Touch and a single pointer | Every control is at least 24 × 24 px. Everything a drag does can be done with single clicks or taps: Zoom in and out, Pan left and right, and Select range for choosing a range with two clicks. A one-finger drag scrolls the page. |\n\nThe legend entries of a line, area, bar or scatter chart are toggle buttons with a pressed state; a hidden series keeps its full-contrast text, struck through. A chart with one series has no legend entries. A donut's legend lists every slice, each with a button that selects that slice (the chart fires `select`), without a pressed state.\n\n## The keyboard map\n\nThe plot is a single native range input laid over the chart. Its keys:\n\n| Key | In the plot |\n|---|---|\n| Left, Right | Previous or next x, with every visible series there. Scatter: the previous or next point in x, then y order. Donut: the previous or next slice. |\n| Home, End | The first or last point. |\n| Page Up, Page Down | Forward or back by one tenth of the number of points, rounded down, and at least one. |\n| Up, Down | Narrow to one series and move to the previous or next series. Donut: the next or previous slice. |\n| Escape | One thing per press, in this order: end a drag; release Select range; close the tooltip or end a pin: the datum on show stays closed until the pointer has reached a different datum, and nothing else opens at once (after Escape from a held tooltip, the datum under the pointer stays closed too); return from one series to all. When none of these applies, the key is left to the page, so a dialog around the chart closes only on an Escape the chart did not use. |\n| Enter, Space | Select the point: the chart fires its `select` event. |\n| `+`, `-`, `0` | Zoom in, zoom out, show everything (date, time and number x). |\n| Shift with Left or Right | Pan the zoomed view. |\n| Wheel | Zoom, only while the plot has focus and never with Ctrl or Meta held. |\n\nThe toolbar holds the controls that apply to the chart: legend toggles, Zoom in, Select range, Zoom out, Pan left, Pan right, Reset zoom, Pause, View as table. It is one tab stop. Inside it the arrow keys move between controls, Home and End go to the first and last, and Enter or Space presses the control. The open table adds the table's scroll region to the tab order, and, when there are more than 100 rows, its pager (previous page, next page and a \"Jump to\" field). The plot's accessible description gives a short version of this map.\n\nWith several charts on a page, an Escape belongs to the chart that has focus or, when focus is in none of them, to the one that showed something last; one press is used by one chart at most.\n\nThis pattern was chosen by reasoning and by inspecting the browsers' accessibility trees, not by testing with screen readers; see [decision 0001](../../../docs/decisions/0001-plot-interaction-pattern.md) and [decision 0004](../../../docs/decisions/0004-tooltip-and-focused-text.md).\n\n## Reading values with a pointer\n\nPointing anywhere in the plot shows what is there, by the chart type's rule: on line and area charts the nearest x, on bars the band under the pointer, on scatter charts the nearest point within 24 px, on a donut the slice under the pointer. What is shown depends on the room the plot has:\n\n| Plot | What pointing shows |\n|---|---|\n| At least 240 × 140 px | A floating tooltip. |\n| Narrower than 240 px or shorter than 140 px | The same content, written as running text (\"x: series value; series value; +2 more\") in a strip of two lines reserved under the plot. The strip covers nothing, and nothing covers it. |\n| So small that the strip would leave the plot under 80 px high | No readout. The datum is highlighted; its values are in the plot's keyboard reading and in the table. |\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
