{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,235p' packages/axylo/test/core/host.ts && sed -n '352,385p;398,483p' packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts && sed -n '21,43p' apps/docs/pages/accessibility.md\"","aggregated_output":"/**\n * A recording host for driving the chart controller in Node (the method of the core review): a manual\n * animation-frame queue, and substitutes for the figure, the renderers and the interaction layer that keep\n * what they were given. Sizes come from a small model of the figure's CSS: the plot gets what the caption\n * and the controls leave of the container.\n */\nimport type { Layout, PlacedText, Scene, TextStyle } from '../../src/core/contracts';\nimport { createController, type ChartKind, type Controller, type Host, type Size } from '../../src/core/controller';\nimport type { FigureModel } from '../../src/dom/figure';\nimport type { Committed, ControlsState } from '../../src/dom/interaction';\nimport { TOKEN_BINDINGS } from '../../src/theme';\n\nexport interface Recording {\n  readonly host: Host;\n  readonly controller: Controller;\n  /** Runs every queued animation frame (and those they queue), at most `limit` rounds. */\n  frames(limit?: number): number;\n  readonly pending: number;\n  draws: Scene[];\n  texts: (readonly PlacedText[])[];\n  models: FigureModel[];\n  announcements: string[];\n  prepared: ControlsState[];\n  committed: Committed | null;\n  commits: number;\n  clears: number;\n  themeCalls: { keys: readonly string[]; colors: Record<string, string> }[];\n  printed: string[];\n  disposed: number;\n  /** Host writes (figure, renderer, text, interaction) made after `dispose`. */\n  writesAfterDispose: number;\n  /** The last surfaces(visible) call: false while the error revision hides marks and text. */\n  surfaces: boolean;\n  /** The container (CSS px). The plot's height is what the caption and the controls leave. */\n  container: { width: number; height: number } | null;\n  /** Height of one caption line and of the controls row in the model of the figure. */\n  readonly lineHeight: number;\n  ids: Record<string, string>;\n  readonly layout: Layout | null;\n}\n\nexport interface HostOptions {\n  readonly container?: { width: number; height: number } | null;\n  readonly console?: boolean;\n  readonly timeZone?: string;\n  readonly locale?: string;\n  readonly textWidth?: Host['measurer']['width'];\n  readonly captionLineHeight?: number;\n  /** The page's `lang` (A10); 'en' when not given. */\n  readonly pageLang?: string;\n  /** The target element's own id (an untitled chart's name in diagnostics). */\n  readonly targetId?: string;\n  /**\n   * The readout strip's real height (two line heights of its own font). When given, a reserved strip takes\n   * that much from the plot's column, as the DOM does, and the host reports the strip's height to the chart.\n   * A function: the height the page's CSS gives it now (responsive CSS can change it with the size).\n   */\n  readonly strip?: number | (() => number);\n  /** The host does not report the strip's height: the chart estimates it from its text style. */\n  readonly stripUnknown?: boolean;\n  /** Called inside the interaction layer's commit, as the DOM layer calls hover while it presents. */\n  readonly onCommit?: (state: Committed, controller: Controller) => void;\n}\n\nexport function record(kind: ChartKind, options: Record<string, unknown>, settings: HostOptions = {}): Recording {\n  const queue = new Map<number, (time?: number) => void>();\n  /** Animation frame time: one value per batch of callbacks, as a browser gives it. */\n  let clock = 0;\n  let handles = 0;\n  const rec = {\n    draws: [] as Scene[], texts: [] as (readonly PlacedText[])[], models: [] as FigureModel[], announcements: [] as string[],\n    prepared: [] as ControlsState[], committed: null as Committed | null, commits: 0, clears: 0,\n    themeCalls: [] as { keys: readonly string[]; colors: Record<string, string> }[], printed: [] as string[], disposed: 0,\n    writesAfterDispose: 0, surfaces: true,\n    container: settings.container === undefined ? { width: 720, height: 400 } : settings.container,\n    lineHeight: settings.captionLineHeight ?? 20, ids: {} as Record<string, string>,\n  };\n  let model: FigureModel | null = null;\n  let controls: ControlsState | null = null;\n  const stripNow = (): number => typeof settings.strip === 'function' ? settings.strip() : settings.strip ?? 0;\n  const style: TextStyle = { font: '400 12px sans-serif', letterSpacing: 0, wordSpacing: 0, lineHeight: 15 };\n\n  /** The plot size the model figure gives: container minus caption (title, subtitle, visible summary) and controls. */\n  function plotSize(): Size | null {\n    const box = rec.container;\n    if (box === null) return null;\n    let used = 0;\n    if (model && !model.compact) {\n      if (model.title?.visible) used += rec.lineHeight;\n      if (model.subtitle) used += rec.lineHeight;\n      if (model.summaryVisible) used += 2 * rec.lineHeight;\n      if (model.note) used += rec.lineHeight;\n    }\n    if (controls && controls.interactive) {\n      // The legend and toolbar take a row; the fallback offers only the table control, which is a row too\n      // but shorter (no legend).\n      used += controls.tooSmall ? rec.lineHeight : 1.5 * rec.lineHeight;\n    }\n    const column = { width: box.width, height: box.height - used };\n    if (settings.strip === undefined) return column;\n    // The strip is in the plot's column: the column (room) stays, the plot gets what the strip leaves.\n    const reserved = controls && (controls as { readout?: boolean }).readout === true ? stripNow() : 0;\n    return { width: column.width, height: column.height - reserved, room: column };\n  }\n\n  const host: Host = {\n    id: 'axylo-test',\n    targetId: settings.targetId ?? null,\n    console: settings.console === false ? null : {\n      warn: (...args: unknown[]) => { rec.printed.push(String(args[0])); },\n      info: (...args: unknown[]) => { rec.printed.push(String(args[0])); },\n      error: (...args: unknown[]) => { rec.printed.push(String(args[0])); },\n    },\n    page: {},\n    timeZone: settings.timeZone ?? 'UTC',\n    renderer: { kind: 'svg', draw: scene => { if (rec.disposed) rec.writesAfterDispose++; rec.draws.push(scene); } },\n    text: { render: texts => { if (rec.disposed) rec.writesAfterDispose++; rec.texts.push(texts); } },\n    surfaces(visible) {\n      rec.surfaces = visible;\n    },\n    figure: {\n      update(next) {\n        if (rec.disposed) rec.writesAfterDispose++;\n        const before = model;\n        model = next;\n        rec.models.push(next);\n        return before === null || before.summaryVisible !== next.summaryVisible || before.note !== next.note ||\n          before.title?.text !== next.title?.text || before.subtitle !== next.subtitle;\n      },\n      announce: text => { rec.announcements.push(text); },\n    },\n    interaction: {\n      prepare(state) {\n        const before = controls;\n        controls = state;\n        rec.prepared.push(state);\n        return before === null || before.tooSmall !== state.tooSmall || before.interactive !== state.interactive;\n      },\n      commit(state) {\n        if (rec.disposed) rec.writesAfterDispose++;\n        rec.committed = state;\n        rec.commits++;\n        if (state) settings.onCommit?.(state, controller);\n      },\n      clear() {\n        rec.committed = null;\n        rec.clears++;\n      },\n    },\n    measurer: { width: settings.textWidth ?? (text => text.length * 7) },\n    requestFrame(callback) {\n      const handle = ++handles;\n      queue.set(handle, callback);\n      return handle;\n    },\n    cancelFrame(handle) {\n      queue.delete(handle);\n    },\n    locale: option => typeof option === 'string' ? option : settings.locale ?? 'en-US',\n    pageLang: () => settings.pageLang ?? 'en',\n    labelText: id => Object.hasOwn(rec.ids, id) ? rec.ids[id]! : null,\n    textStyle: () => style,\n    measure: plotSize,\n    ...(settings.strip === undefined || settings.stripUnknown ? {} : { stripHeight: stripNow }),\n    devicePixelRatio: () => 1,\n    theme(keys, colors) {\n      rec.themeCalls.push({ keys: [...keys], colors });\n      const series = keys.map((_, i) => `var(--axylo-series-color-${i + 1})`);\n      const paints = { tokens: { ...TOKEN_BINDINGS }, series };\n      return {\n        bindings: { tokens: TOKEN_BINDINGS, series },\n        theme: { scheme: 'light', forcedColors: false, moreContrast: false, paints },\n        resolved: true, backdropKnown: false,\n      };\n    },\n    dispose() {\n      rec.disposed++;\n    },\n  };\n\n  const controller = createController(kind, options, host);\n  // Accessors stay accessors: `pending` and `layout` are read when asked (review 3, finding 20).\n  return Object.defineProperties(Object.assign(rec, {\n    host, controller,\n    frames(limit = 10): number {\n      let rounds = 0;\n      while (queue.size && rounds < limit) {\n        rounds++;\n        const callbacks = [...queue.values()];\n        queue.clear();\n        clock += 16;\n        for (const cb of callbacks) cb(clock);\n      }\n      return rounds;\n    },\n  }), {\n    pending: { get: () => queue.size, enumerable: true },\n    layout: { get: () => rec.committed?.layout ?? null, enumerable: true },\n  }) as unknown as Recording;\n}\n\nexport const lastModel = (r: Recording): FigureModel => r.models[r.models.length - 1]!;\n * that string in the scenarios below, or says why none does.\n */\nconst WHERE: Record<keyof Messages, readonly ChartType[] | string> = {\n  viewAsTable: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'], hideTable: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'],\n  noData: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'], noObservation: ['line', 'area', 'bar'], incompleteStack: ['area', 'bar'],\n  moreRows: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter'], otherSlices: ['donut'], valuesNotShown: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut', 'compact'],\n  valuesChanged: ['donut'], labelsHidden: 'only when labels do not fit after every remedy; not reached by these fixtures',\n  loading: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut', 'compact'], empty: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut', 'compact'],\n  error: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut', 'compact'], internalError: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut', 'compact'],\n  chartName: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut', 'compact'], chartSummary: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'compact'],\n  seriesSummary: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'compact'],\n  timeZoneNote: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'compact'], plotLabel: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'],\n  controlsLabel: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'], pointOf: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter'],\n  zoomIn: ['line', 'area', 'scatter'], zoomOut: ['line', 'area', 'scatter'], resetZoom: ['line', 'area', 'scatter'],\n  pause: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'], resume: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'],\n  previousPage: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'], nextPage: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'], pageOf: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'],\n  jumpToX: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'],\n  category: ['donut'], percentage: ['donut'], series: ['scatter'], value: 'used only when a value field has no label; every scenario labels or names it',\n  typeLine: ['line', 'compact'], typeArea: ['area'], typeBar: ['bar'], typeScatter: ['scatter'], typeDonut: ['donut'],\n  donutSummary: ['donut'], seriesNoData: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter'], seriesNotDrawn: ['line', 'area', 'bar'],\n  referenceLine: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter'], referenceBand: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter'],\n  plotRole: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'], pointAll: ['line', 'area', 'bar'], seriesValue: ['line', 'area', 'bar'],\n  position: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'donut'], total: ['area', 'bar'], panLeft: ['line', 'area', 'scatter'], panRight: ['line', 'area', 'scatter'],\n  // totalMixed: a mixed-sign stack's readout (spec F10). incompleteAt and incompleteCount are summary templates\n  // for charts that have no tooltip or table, the compact kinds (src/reader/index.ts uses them there); on full\n  // area and bar charts an incomplete stack is marked through incompleteStack in tooltip, table and value text.\n  // The compact scenario below exercises compact area and compact bar for them.\n  totalMixed: ['area', 'bar'], incompleteAt: ['compact'], incompleteCount: ['compact'],\n  // selectRange: the toolbar toggle for two-click range selection, shown wherever drag-to-zoom is (as Zoom in).\n  selectRange: ['line', 'area', 'scatter'],\n  jumpNotFound: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'], plotInstructions: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'], seeTable: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'],\n};\nconst KEYS = Object.keys(WHERE) as (keyof Messages)[];\n/** Each key's own sentinel, with every placeholder the templates use, so filled templates stay recognisable. */\n/** Scenarios that between them bring every applicable built-in string of `type` onto a reader surface. */\nasync function exercise(page: Page, type: ChartType): Promise<string> {\n  const seen: string[] = [];\n  const fresh = async (fn: string, options: Record<string, unknown>) => {\n    await page.evaluate(() => { for (const c of (window as unknown as { charts: { destroy(): void }[] }).charts.splice(0)) c.destroy(); });\n    await createRaw(page, fn, { ...options, messages: MESSAGES });\n  };\n  const take = async () => { seen.push(await surfaces(page)); };\n  const aligned = type === 'line' || type === 'area' || type === 'bar';\n  const fn = type === 'compact' ? 'line' : type;\n  const compact = type === 'compact' ? { compact: true } : {};\n  const DAY = 864e5, T0 = Date.UTC(2026, 2, 2);\n  // 1. Instants with a null, a series with no row at one x, a series with no data, a duplicate x in a series, references; no title.\n  if (type === 'donut') {\n    await fresh('donut', { data: [{ l: 'A', v: 30 }, { l: 'B', v: null }, { l: 'C', v: '__NaN__' }, ...Array.from({ length: 8 }, (_, i) => ({ l: `S${i}`, v: 10 - i }))], label: 'l', value: 'v' });\n  } else if (type === 'scatter') {\n    await fresh('scatter', { data: [{ x: T0, y: 1, s: 'A' }, { x: T0 + DAY, y: null, s: 'A' }, { x: T0 + 2 * DAY, y: '__NaN__', s: 'A' }, { x: T0, y: 2, s: 'Z' }, { x: T0, y: null, s: 'E' }], x: { field: 'x', type: 'time', timeZone: 'UTC' }, y: 'y', series: 's', reference: [{ y: 1.5, label: 'Mid' }, { y: [0.5, 0.8], label: 'Low' }] });\n  } else {\n    const rows = [\n      { x: T0, s: 'A', y: 1 }, { x: T0 + DAY, s: 'A', y: null }, { x: T0 + 2 * DAY, s: 'A', y: 3 }, { x: T0 + 3 * DAY, s: 'A', y: '__NaN__' },\n      { x: T0, s: 'B', y: 2 }, { x: T0 + 2 * DAY, s: 'B', y: 4 }, { x: T0 + 3 * DAY, s: 'B', y: 5 },\n      { x: T0, s: 'E', y: null }, { x: T0, s: 'D', y: 1 }, { x: T0, s: 'D', y: 2 },\n      // A negative component, so a stacked readout has a positive and a negative total (totalMixed).\n      { x: T0 + 2 * DAY, s: 'C', y: -2 },\n    ];\n    await fresh(fn, { data: type === 'compact' ? rows.filter(r => r.s === 'A') : rows, x: { field: 'x', type: 'time', timeZone: 'UTC' }, y: 'y', ...(type === 'compact' ? {} : { series: 's' }), ...compact, ...(type === 'compact' ? {} : { reference: [{ y: 1.5, label: 'Mid' }, { x: [T0 + DAY, T0 + 2 * DAY], label: 'Window' }] }), ...((type === 'area' || type === 'bar') ? (type === 'area' ? { stacked: true } : { layout: 'stacked' }) : {}) });\n  }\n  await take();\n  if (type === 'compact') {\n    // Compact area and compact bar, stacked with a missing component: the summary says the stacks are incomplete.\n    // One incomplete stack is named by position (incompleteAt); many are counted (incompleteCount,\n    // src/reader/index.ts: more than MAX_STACK_POSITIONS).\n    for (const kind of ['area', 'bar'] as const) {\n      for (const incomplete of [1, 12]) {\n        const xs = Array.from({ length: 14 }, (_, k) => `c${k}`);\n        const data = xs.flatMap((x, k) => [{ x, s: 'P', y: 1 + k }, ...(k > 0 && k <= incomplete ? [] : [{ x, s: 'Q', y: 2 }])]);\n        await fresh(kind, { compact: true, data, x: 'x', y: 'y', series: 's', ...(kind === 'area' ? { stacked: true } : { layout: 'stacked' }) });\n        await take();\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  if (type !== 'compact') {\n    // 2. Keyboard over the null and the missing row, tooltip on them, the table with a failed jump.\n    await page.focus('#chart .axylo-proxy');\n    for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) { await page.keyboard.press('ArrowRight'); await take(); }\n    await page.keyboard.press('ArrowDown');\n    await take();\n    const p = await box(page, '#chart .axylo-proxy');\n    for (const f of [0.02, 0.35, 0.65, 0.98]) { await page.mouse.move(p.x + f * p.width, p.y + p.height / 2); await settle(page); await take(); }\n    // Off the plot first: whether the readout may cover a control is I1's question (i1-pointer), not this one's.\n    await page.mouse.move(0, 0);\n    await page.focus('#before');\n    await settle(page);\n    await page.locator('#chart [role=\"toolbar\"] button').last().click();\n    await settle(page);\n    await take();\n    // 3. Paging (250 rows), zoom and pan, streaming and pause, more than eight rows in a tooltip.\n    const many = type === 'donut' ? { data: Array.from({ length: 250 }, (_, k) => ({ l: `c${k}`, v: k + 1 })), label: 'l', value: 'v' }\n      : type === 'scatter' ? { data: [...Array.from({ length: 250 }, (_, k) => ({ x: k, y: k % 7, s: 'S0' })), ...Array.from({ length: 10 }, (_, k) => ({ x: 100, y: 3, s: `S${k + 1}` }))], x: 'x', y: 'y', series: 's' }\n        : { data: Array.from({ length: 250 }, (_, k) => Array.from({ length: 10 }, (_, s) => ({ x: type === 'bar' ? `c${k}` : k, s: `S${s}`, y: k + s }))).flat(), x: 'x', y: 'y', series: 's' };\n    await fresh(fn, { title: 'Many', ...many });\n    await page.locator('#chart [role=\"toolbar\"] button').last().click();\n    await settle(page);\n    await page.locator('#chart .axylo-pager button').last().click();\n    await settle(page);\n    await take();\n    await page.locator('#chart .axylo-jump-field').click();\n    await page.keyboard.type('no such value');\n    await page.keyboard.press('Enter');\n    await settle(page);\n    await take();\n    // Close the table again, so the plot is back under the pointer.\n    await page.locator('#chart [role=\"toolbar\"] button').last().click();\n    await settle(page);\n    if (type === 'line' || type === 'area' || type === 'scatter') {\n      await page.mouse.move(0, 0);\n      for (const k of ['zoomIn', 'panLeft'] as const) {\n        const b = page.locator('#chart [role=\"toolbar\"] button', { hasText: sentinel(k) });\n        if (await b.count() !== 1) throw new Error(`no ${k} control`);\n        await b.click({ timeout: 10000 });\n        await settle(page);\n      }\n      await take();\n    }\n    const q = await box(page, '#chart .axylo-proxy');\n    // More than eight rows: the coincident scatter points (series S1…S10 at one place), or ten series at one x.\n## The keyboard map\n\nThe plot is a single native range input laid over the chart. Its keys:\n\n| Key | In the plot |\n|---|---|\n| Left, Right | Previous or next x, with every visible series there. Scatter: the previous or next point in x, then y order. Donut: the previous or next slice. |\n| Home, End | The first or last point. |\n| Page Up, Page Down | Forward or back by one tenth of the number of points, rounded down, and at least one. |\n| Up, Down | Narrow to one series and move to the previous or next series. Donut: the next or previous slice. |\n| Escape | One thing per press, in this order: end a drag; release Select range; close the tooltip or end a pin: the datum on show stays closed until the pointer has reached a different datum, and nothing else opens at once (after Escape from a held tooltip, the datum under the pointer stays closed too); return from one series to all. When none of these applies, the key is left to the page, so a dialog around the chart closes only on an Escape the chart did not use. |\n| Enter, Space | Select the point: the chart fires its `select` event. |\n| `+`, `-`, `0` | Zoom in, zoom out, show everything (date, time and number x). |\n| Shift with Left or Right | Pan the zoomed view. |\n| Wheel | Zoom, only while the plot has focus and never with Ctrl or Meta held. |\n\nThe toolbar holds the controls that apply to the chart: legend toggles, Zoom in, Select range, Zoom out, Pan left, Pan right, Reset zoom, Pause, View as table. It is one tab stop. Inside it the arrow keys move between controls, Home and End go to the first and last, and Enter or Space presses the control. The open table adds the table's scroll region to the tab order, and, when there are more than 100 rows, its pager (previous page, next page and a \"Jump to\" field). The plot's accessible description gives a short version of this map.\n\nWith several charts on a page, an Escape belongs to the chart that has focus or, when focus is in none of them, to the one that showed something last; one press is used by one chart at most.\n\nThis pattern was chosen by reasoning and by inspecting the browsers' accessibility trees, not by testing with screen readers; see [decision 0001](../../../docs/decisions/0001-plot-interaction-pattern.md) and [decision 0004](../../../docs/decisions/0004-tooltip-and-focused-text.md).\n\n## Reading values with a pointer\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
